# =============================================================================
# experiment/tgrad/tgrad_T-20_h1.00_G0_rhovHiLo_beta1.00x.opts
#
# MIRROR CONTROL for the beta_sub0 sweep. Identical to
# tgrad_T-20_h1.00_G0_rhovHiLo_beta1.00x.opts except that -rhovfix_lo and
# -rhovfix_hi are exchanged.
#
# Pair with geometry/wedge/wedge_2D_L300um_eps0.86um_90deg_mirror.opts, which
# reflects the channel about x = Lx/2: the wide end moves to x=0, the throat to
# x=Lx, and the virtual apex to (4.0e-04, 1.0e-04). Reflecting the geometry
# without also exchanging the two reservoirs would change the physics rather
# than mirror it, since -rhovfix_lo is tied to the x=0 face and that face is now
# the WIDE end.
#
# EXPECTED RESULT: the two menisci exchange roles exactly. The inner (concave)
# meniscus is now on the right, so the mirrored run's OUTER-meniscus numbers
# should reproduce the unmirrored run's INNER ones and vice versa, to within the
# quoted sigma-extraction sensitivity. The unmirrored 1.00x arm shows a residual
# ~1% difference between the two menisci; this run determines whether that
# difference follows the geometry (concave vs convex, hence physical) or the
# side (left vs right, hence an artifact of the mesh or the measurement).
#
# The thin-interface counter-terms were removed from tau_sub on 2026-09-09
# (-thin_iface_corr, default 0). Before that change the realised kinetic
# coefficient was beta_sub0 + Delta rather than beta_sub0, and this sweep
# measured the resulting shortfall as 0.3160 / 0.5359 / 0.8220 / 0.9487 across
# the four arms (batch 2026-08-25__18.14.15_beta_ladder). With the correction
# removed the prediction for EVERY arm is
#
#     v_n,measured / v_n,predicted  =  1.0000
#
# so the four arms together test that the fix holds over a 40x range in
# beta_sub0, not merely at one point. Read the ratio from each run's
# postprocess/wedge_gt_velocity.py summary.
#
# THIS ARM: beta_sub0 = 5.9216e+05 s/m  (1x the reference 5.9216e+05)
#           tau_sub   = 429.21 s   (was 522.13 s before the fix)
#
# -t_final and -dtmax are recomputed for the corrected tau_sub: v_n now scales
# as 1/beta_sub0 rather than 1/(beta_sub0 + Delta), so both had to move. They
# are set so every arm runs the same 3406 steps and moves the menisci the
# same ~2 control-point spacings, giving all four equal cost and equal precision.
#   -dtmax   = 1.093 * tau_sub
#   -t_final scales with beta_sub0
# =============================================================================

-t_final 1.5980e+06                     # 18.50 d

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0                  # isothermal: geometry and the BCs are the only drivers

-flag_BC_Tfix 1                          # pin wall temperatures (uniform)
-flag_BC_rhovfix 1                       # vapour reservoirs...
-rhovfix_axis 0                          # ...on the x-faces ONLY (open pore ends)
-rhovfix_lo 0.999995                     # rho_v at x=0  / rho_vs
-rhovfix_hi 1.000005                     # rho_v at x=Lx / rho_vs

-beta_sub0 5.9216e+05                   # 1x reference; predicted ratio 1.0000
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                        # physical capillary length at -20 C

-dtmax 4.691e+02                        # 1.093 * tau_sub (429.2 s)
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2
